# ── secrets: never commit ──────────────────────────────
#
# Case matters, and it nearly cost us. `*credentials*` alone does NOT match
# CREDENTIALS.md on a case-sensitive filesystem — it matched on this Windows box
# only because core.ignorecase=true. Every Linux checkout, CI runner and GitHub
# Action loses the protection, and the 2026-08-17 near-miss (StartUp.md §13) was
# stopped by a control that only works on one developer's machine. Globs here are
# spelled case-insensitively rather than trusting the filesystem.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.p8
*.jks
*.keystore
auth.json
oauth2*.json

# Service-account keys, added 2026-09-09 after the Android session measured the
# guard above and found it open where it mattered most. `*credential*` and
# `*secret*` catch the names somebody INVENTS; they catch none of the names a
# console actually HANDS you. Firebase downloads `firebase-adminsdk-*.json` and
# Google Cloud downloads `<project-id>-<hash>.json`, and neither contains the
# word credential or secret. A key that is silently ignored is a nuisance; a key
# silently committed is a rotation and a service reset.
#
# google-services.json is deliberately NOT matched here: it carries no private
# key, it belongs in the tree, and the Android build fails at configuration time
# without it.
*service-account*.json
*serviceaccount*.json
*adminsdk*.json
ezbizi-506117-*.json
.netrc
.npmrc
id_rsa*
*[Cc][Rr][Ee][Dd][Ee][Nn][Tt][Ii][Aa][Ll]*
*[Ss][Ee][Cc][Rr][Ee][Tt]*
*.stackdump

# Stray sqlite databases from the DB_DATABASE trap. `DB_DATABASE=x artisan ...`
# outside the test runner names a FILE, not a schema, because .env says sqlite —
# so it silently creates one here and exits 0 listing every migration as run.
# A 925 KB `ezbizi_testing_twilio` was sitting in this directory, untracked and
# unignored, when this rule was written. See docs/ACTIVE-CONSTRAINTS.md.
ezbizi_testing*
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
database/*.db

# ── dependencies / build ──────────────────────────────
/vendor
/composer.phar
/node_modules
/public/build
/public/hot
/public/storage
/storage/*.key
/storage/framework/cache/*
/storage/framework/sessions/*
/storage/framework/views/*
/storage/logs/*
!/storage/**/.gitkeep

# ── local ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.superpowers/
.worktrees/
.cursor/agent-mail-stall.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log

# Flutter web build output — derived, not source. Built locally and uploaded to
# the shared directory on the server (see scripts/deploy.sh). 36 MB per build,
# almost all CanvasKit, and a new blob on every rebuild: committing it would
# bloat the repo permanently for no gain.
/public/app

# Release artefacts — installers and app bundles, produced by scripts/release.sh.
# Derived from a commit, tens of MB each, and a fresh blob on every build. They
# are uploaded to Play and handed to testers, not versioned here.
/Distribution

# PHPUnit's test-result cache. Rewritten by every run, so tracking it made the
# tree dirty after any test and blocked release.sh. Laravel gitignores it by
# default; this repo had it committed.
.phpunit.result.cache

# Scratch output from the Playwright MCP browser. Session artefacts, never source.
/.playwright-mcp/

# App Store screenshots, produced by scripts/screenshots-ios.sh from the real
# app on a simulator. Derived output: 2.7 MB of PNGs that this repo would push
# to the production server on every deploy, and that any machine with the
# simulator can regenerate.
# Unanchored on purpose. This was `/store-screenshots/`, which only matches the
# repository root - but `flutter drive` runs in client/, so the screenshots land
# in client/store-screenshots/ and were never ignored at all. Two megabytes of
# PNGs, one `git add -A` from being committed, behind a rule everyone believed
# was covering them.
store-screenshots/

# Laravel's schema dump. NOT committed, deliberately.
#
# It makes the server's deploy gate much faster — one file load instead of
# replaying 82 migrations, each paying two fsyncs on a busy disk. But Laravel
# LOADS it by shelling out to the `mysql` client, and on the Windows dev
# machines the MySQL bin directory is not on PATH, so every local test run dies
# with "'mysql' is not recognized" the moment this file exists.
#
# Breaking every developer's local loop to speed up one server step is the wrong
# trade. The deploy dying was never this anyway — that was an SSH idle timeout,
# fixed with ServerAliveInterval. Revisit if the bin dir gets onto PATH and
# DEV-ENVIRONMENT.md says so.
/database/schema/

# ── repo hygiene (2026-11-25): personal data and signing material ─────────
# The repo is being prepared to go public. See docs/security/ and
# scripts/hooks/pre-commit, which blocks the same things at commit time.
# Signing keys and their property files (Android upload key, Apple .p8/.p12).
key.properties
**/android/key.properties
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p8
*.p12
*.pem
*.mobileprovision
# Local credential folders, whatever their case (the F:\Credentials junction).
[Cc]redentials/
**/[Cc]redentials/
# Spreadsheet and CSV exports dropped into docs/ are customer data until
# proven otherwise. A canonical config CSV is tracked by name below.
docs/**/*.xlsx
docs/**/*.xls
docs/**/*.csv
docs/**/*.tsv
!docs/agents/task-labels-canonical-2026-11-19.csv
# Database dumps and call/recording exports.
*.sql.gz
*.dump
# The CI scan's own workflow file matches the *secret* rule above; it holds no secret.
!.github/workflows/secret-scan.yml
